#
# holt — Crystal for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract Crystal symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `Crystal`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own Crystal parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"Crystal\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### Crystal ####################################################################
--langdef=HoltCrystal
--map-HoltCrystal=+.cr
--kinddef-HoltCrystal=f,function,methods
--kinddef-HoltCrystal=c,class,classes and modules
--regex-HoltCrystal=/^[ \t]*def[ \t]+(self\.)?([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*[?!=]?)/\2/f/
--regex-HoltCrystal=/^[ \t]*(class|module|struct|enum|lib)[ \t]+([A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_:]*)/\2/c/
